{"ts":1793369308259,"event":"done","summary":"PLAT-103 shipped. shared-contracts 2.0.0 (PR #1): validateApp throws when app.owner is missing or empty. Major bump because it is a breaking change for callers. Apps moved to ^2.0.0 and pass their owning team from package.json: core-shell=platform (PR #2), sub-route-billing=payments (PR #3), sub-route-reports=insights (PR #4). All four CI and CD runs are green. Assumptions: (1) owner is hardcoded in each app's source to match package.json team, not read from package.json at build time. (2) Major bump rather than minor, so apps on ^1.0.0 keep working until they move. (3) platform-kit does not call validateApp, so it is untouched. (4) st deps lists only shell and billing as consumers, but sub-route-reports also depends on @mfe/shared-contracts, so the catalog is stale."}
